  "provenance": {
    "generators": "serene/testing/synthetic.py uses seed-derived SHA-256 ids, a fixed clock and scripted reports; tests/conftest.py constructs SyntheticFamily only.",
    "eval": "eval/README.md declares all child data synthetic. runtime_scenarios.py defines REPORTS and QUESTION; runtime_live.py imports them and ParentSim returns scenario facts. Archived model-generated narratives derive from those inputs, not live family records.",
    "web": "The current main frontend is an empty-state shell. Its causal-twin fixture uses sequential ids and synthetic-fixture model provenance; the fixture route is build-gated. Its memory/Dream fixture (#36) is kernel output, not hand-written: tests/memory_view_fixture.py runs build_full_ladder(seed='memory-dream-fixture') (SyntheticFamily, fixed clock), a ScriptedModelDreamer with synthetic model provenance and a temporary Git memory repo, and tests/test_memory_view.py pins the bytes; it holds no child or actor ids; the fixture route is build-gated. Its experiments fixture and approval-command example (#37) are kernel output: tests/experiments_view_fixture.py drives SyntheticFamily(seed='experiments-fixture') through the real lifecycle service into every phase, with each parent decision made through WebApprovalChannel; tests/test_experiments_view.py and tests/test_web_approvals.py pin the bytes; no child or actor ids; the fixture route and its scripted transport are build-gated. Its investigation fixture (#35) is kernel output: tests/investigation_view_fixture.py runs the investigation controller over a synthetic family (make_investigation_rig, scripted Hermes replies, Telegram script) and records the projection_state rows the after-append hook would publish; tests/test_investigation_view.py pins the bytes; no raw report text or actor ids; the fixture routes are build-gated.",
    "fixtures": "Pinned daycare/holdout pages are fictional public-evidence stand-ins. Provider auth/error fixtures retain sanitized technical responses and synthetic model proposals, not credentials or family input.",
    "names": "Names including Maya in test examples and historical narratives are fictional scenario labels. A name alone is neither evidence of real PII nor proof of synthetic origin; provenance is the generator and reviewed bytes.",
    "maya_demo": "Merged #56/#57 canonical Maya demo: fixed fictional seed maya-daycare-pickup-v1, SyntheticFamily, scripted model/browser I/O, synthetic report marker and temporary memory repository. Reset accepts only the canonical seed. Offline webhook stand-in is fingerprint-allowlisted, never used as a live credential. Implementation unchanged by #59.",
    "maya_web_demo": "docs/maya-demo.md adds local recording and verification instructions for the opt-in canonical report adapter. No scenario facts, generators, kernel behaviour or reviewed fixture bytes change. The web route reads only the existing synthetic report; it creates no additional result fixture. Production sign-in and web approval transport remain open.",
    "controlled_dev_1": "eval/fixtures/controlled-dev-1.json and eval/reports/archive/2026-10-12-controlled-dev-1/ hold protocol parameters, tape digests, scorer/trust-scorer metrics, reason codes, token counts and NeatLogs receipt ids from the synthetic DEV scenarios; no model prose, parent text or family records (reviewed 2026-10-12)."
  },
